      "pot": {
        "content": "```python\ndef solution():\n    # Define variables\n    stock_price = 150.0\n    strike_price = 140.0\n    time_to_expiration = 0.5\n    risk_free_rate = 0.02\n    volatility = 0.25\n\n    # Do math calculation to get the answer\n    from math import log, sqrt, exp, erf\n\n    def normal_cdf(x):\n        return 0.5 * (1.0 + erf(x / sqrt(2.0)))\n\n    d1 = (\n        log(stock_price / strike_price)\n        + (risk_free_rate + 0.5 * volatility ** 2) * time_to_expiration\n    ) / (volatility * sqrt(time_to_expiration))\n\n    d2 = d1 - volatility * sqrt(time_to_expiration)\n\n    put_price = (\n        strike_price * exp(-risk_free_rate * time_to_expiration) * normal_cdf(-d2)\n        - stock_price * normal_cdf(-d1)\n    )\n\n    # Return the fair price rounded to two decimal places\n    return round(put_price, 2)\n```",
